<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: SKI JUMPING-LEADING WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SKI JUMPING-LEADING WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>HARRACHOV, Czech Republic 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading results</p>
<p>in a world cup high hill (120 metres) ski jumping event on</p>
<p>Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Primoz Peterka (Slovenia) 236.1 points (first jump</p>
<p>115/second 121.5)</p>
<p> 2. Andreas Goldberger (Austria) 231.0 (113.5/124)</p>
<p> 3. Kristian Brenden (Norway)    223.5 (119/116)</p>
<p> 4. Adam Malysz (Poland)	   208.4 (108.5/107)</p>
<p> 5. Mika Laitinen (Finland)	204.8 (103.5/122.5)</p>
<p> 6. Dieter Thoma (Germany)	 203.8 (100/123.5)</p>
<p> 7. Hiroya Saitoh (Japan)	  203.5 (102/123)</p>
<p> 8. Robert Krenek (Czech Rep)    202.5 (103.5/121)</p>
<p> 9. Lasse Ottesen (Norway)	 201.9 (99/124)</p>
<p>10. Jaroslav Sakala (Czech Rep) 193.8 (96/122.5)</p>
<p>Leading World Cup standings (after six events):</p>
<p> 1. Peterka			    365 points</p>
<p> 2. Brenden			    311</p>
<p> 3. Goldberger			 292</p>
<p> 4. Thoma				279</p>
<p> 5. Takanobu Okabe (Japan)	 275</p>
<p> 6. Kazuyoshi Funaki (Japan)     261</p>
<p> 7. Saitoh			     233</p>
<p> 8. Ottesen			    188</p>
<p>9. Ari-Pekka Nikkola (Finland)  181</p>
<p> 10. Espen Bredesen (Norway)     128</p>
